<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en" data-theme="light"><head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; script-src-attr 'none'; style-src 'self'; style-src-attr 'none'; connect-src 'none'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'">
  <title>S145 — Repeated transition and soak rehearsal</title>
  <script src="theme.js"></script>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
  <script src="model.js" defer=""></script>
  <script src="lesson.js" defer=""></script>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#controls">Skip to operator controls</a>
  <header>
    <p id="training-banner" class="banner">Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result</p>
    <h1>S145 — Repeated transitions and soak</h1>
    <p>Repeat a bounded swap / rollback sequence. Inspect cumulative memory, connection and cache trends separately from complete-journey correctness.</p>
    <p class="limit">Every cycle, version, connection, memory/cache value, resource, load, metric, budget, journey, failure and recovery below is <strong>fixed fictional teaching DATA ONLY</strong>. No live process, storage, network, load generator, cloud or user-data operations occur.</p>
  </header>
  <main>
    <section aria-labelledby="guide-title">
      <h2 id="guide-title">Declare → conduct → inspect → measure</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Choose a fixed trace and begin. The same original fleet baseline and four-cycle declaration apply throughout the attempt.</li>
        <li>Conduct one cycle at a time. Inspect absolute samples, original-baseline growth, intended versions and original journey outcomes.</li>
        <li>Measure the whole sequence. Equality is allowed; a small per-cycle increment or successful final cycle does not excuse accumulated growth.</li>
        <li>Cancel a segment to inspect preserved evidence, then resume. Archive and reset keeps every previous attempt and measurement; session failures and unknowns cannot be laundered.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Fixed envelope: 4 journeys per cycle, 150 fictional ms per original journey; growth limits +8 fictional MiB, +4 connections, +8 cache entries at the same fixed post-drain point. These are lesson-specific thresholds, not infrastructure recommendations.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="operator-title">
      <h2 id="operator-title">Operator console</h2>
      <form id="controls" novalidate="">
        <label for="trace">Fixed teaching trace</label>
        <select id="trace" name="trace" aria-describedby="trace-help"><option value="threshold-equality">Growth exactly at all limits</option><option value="steady">Steady repeated swap / rollback</option><option value="memory-growth">Small increments, cumulative memory growth</option><option value="connection-growth">Small increments, cumulative connection growth</option><option value="cache-growth">Small increments, cumulative cache growth</option><option value="recovered-growth">Earlier growth breach, latest resources recovered</option><option value="interrupted-recovered">151 ms interruption, separate later recovery</option><option value="unknown-recovered">Unknown original journey, later usable again</option><option value="unknown-cycle">c2 cycle evidence missing</option><option value="unknown-metric">c2 memory sample missing</option><option value="missing-baseline">Original memory baseline missing</option><option value="failed-and-unknown">Earlier interruption and missing memory evidence</option></select>
        <p id="trace-help">Whole-sequence equality passes. Native keyboard controls: arrows, Tab / Shift+Tab, Enter / Space.</p>
        <button id="begin-run" type="submit">Begin declared sequence</button>
      </form>
      <div class="actions">
        <button id="conduct-cycle" type="button" disabled="">Conduct next cycle</button>
        <button id="cancel-segment" type="button" disabled="">Cancel segment, preserve evidence</button>
        <button id="resume-segment" type="button" disabled="">Resume same sequence</button>
        <button id="measure-soak" type="button" disabled="">Measure cumulative outcome</button>
        <button id="archive-reset" type="button">Archive and reset controls</button>
      </div>
      <p id="error" class="error" role="alert" tabindex="-1"></p>
      <p id="segment" role="status" aria-live="polite">No active sequence | Archived 0 / 12 attempts.</p>
      <p id="baseline">Original fictional baseline baseline-145: memory 100, connections 8, cache 20. Same fixed load and post-drain sample boundary; never reset between cycles.</p>
      <p id="verdict" class="verdict" aria-live="polite">UNMEASURED — conduct, inspect, then measure the current revision; earlier measurements remain below.</p>
      <p id="session-verdict">UNKNOWN — cumulative retained session evidence (not a live result)</p>
      <p id="journey-counts">Attempted 0 | Uninterrupted 0 | Interrupted 0 | Unknown 0 | Not attempted 0</p>
      <p id="session-counts">Session attempts 0 | Declared cycles 0 | Conducted 0 | Attempted journeys 0 | Interrupted 0 | Unknown 0</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="trace-title">
      <h2 id="trace-title">Entire declared cycle sequence</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable cycle trace">
        <table>
          <caption>Absolute fictional resource samples and original journey outcomes; missing evidence is not zero.</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Cycle / epoch</th><th scope="col">Intended movement</th><th scope="col">Evidence</th><th scope="col">MiB / connections / cache entries</th><th scope="col">Original journeys</th><th scope="col">Recovery, separate from original</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="cycle-rows"><tr data-cycle="c1"><td>c1 / E145-1</td><td>swap: v1 → v2</td><td>Not conducted; evidence pending</td><td>UNKNOWN / UNKNOWN / UNKNOWN</td><td>NOT ATTEMPTED — no outcome inferred</td><td>No recovery observation</td></tr><tr data-cycle="c2"><td>c2 / E145-2</td><td>rollback: v2 → v1</td><td>Not conducted; evidence pending</td><td>UNKNOWN / UNKNOWN / UNKNOWN</td><td>NOT ATTEMPTED — no outcome inferred</td><td>No recovery observation</td></tr><tr data-cycle="c3"><td>c3 / E145-3</td><td>swap: v1 → v2</td><td>Not conducted; evidence pending</td><td>UNKNOWN / UNKNOWN / UNKNOWN</td><td>NOT ATTEMPTED — no outcome inferred</td><td>No recovery observation</td></tr><tr data-cycle="c4"><td>c4 / E145-4</td><td>rollback: v2 → v1</td><td>Not conducted; evidence pending</td><td>UNKNOWN / UNKNOWN / UNKNOWN</td><td>NOT ATTEMPTED — no outcome inferred</td><td>No recovery observation</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h3>Cumulative resource checks</h3>
      <p>Growth = sample − original baseline; cumulative growth = max(0, all declared growth samples). It is <code>null</code> if a required sample or baseline is missing. A known breach remains FAIL even if later samples recover or other evidence is unknown.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable cumulative resource checks">
        <table>
          <caption>Latest growth and maximum known growth are diagnostics, not substitutes for complete cumulative evidence.</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Metric</th><th scope="col">Original baseline</th><th scope="col">Latest growth</th><th scope="col">Max known growth</th><th scope="col">Cumulative growth</th><th scope="col">Growth limit (inclusive)</th><th scope="col">Missing evidence</th><th scope="col">Check</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="metric-rows"><tr data-metric="memoryMiB" data-status="UNKNOWN"><td>memoryMiB (fictional MiB)</td><td>100</td><td>UNKNOWN (null)</td><td>UNKNOWN (null)</td><td>UNKNOWN (null)</td><td>8</td><td>All cycles pending</td><td>UNKNOWN</td></tr><tr data-metric="connections" data-status="UNKNOWN"><td>connections (fictional connections)</td><td>8</td><td>UNKNOWN (null)</td><td>UNKNOWN (null)</td><td>UNKNOWN (null)</td><td>4</td><td>All cycles pending</td><td>UNKNOWN</td></tr><tr data-metric="cacheEntries" data-status="UNKNOWN"><td>cacheEntries (fictional cache entries)</td><td>20</td><td>UNKNOWN (null)</td><td>UNKNOWN (null)</td><td>UNKNOWN (null)</td><td>8</td><td>All cycles pending</td><td>UNKNOWN</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="limit">Fictional trends cannot establish real leak causality. Successful throughput cannot supply missing memory evidence. A small sample is not five-nines certification, actual Azure migration, production Node.js 24 proof or completion of D-S145.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="history-title">
      <h2 id="history-title">Retained measurements and archived attempts</h2>
      <p>At most 12 attempts and 6 journal actions per attempt. No old record is truncated to admit more work. Archive/reset is in-memory control reset, not real resource cleanup. Reload starts a new teaching session; no storage or durable-soak claim is made.</p>
      <ol id="measurement-history" aria-label="Retained measurements"></ol>
      <ol id="history" aria-label="Complete archived attempts"></ol>
      <details>
        <summary>Inspect exact cumulative output, all journals and retained evidence</summary>
        <pre id="records">{
  "disclaimer": "FIXED FICTIONAL TEACHING DATA ONLY",
  "activeRun": null,
  "assessment": null,
  "session": {
    "attempts": 0,
    "maxAttempts": 12,
    "declaredCycles": 0,
    "conductedCycles": 0,
    "attemptedJourneys": 0,
    "uninterrupted": 0,
    "interrupted": 0,
    "unknown": 0,
    "notAttempted": 0,
    "verdict": "UNKNOWN",
    "limit": "Every baseline and declared sequence is retained; a separately successful/reset cycle is not a whole-session pass."
  },
  "archivedAttempts": [],
  "retainedMeasurements": [],
  "sourceParentAcceptance": "Pending original native and parent gates; no source-parent completion.",
  "cleanup": "In-memory control reset only; no live resources exist or are cleaned up."
}</pre>
      </details>
    </section>
  </main>
  <footer><a href="README.md">Lesson instructions, exact output contract and native remainder</a></footer>
  <noscript>This lesson needs local JavaScript. No result is verified with scripting disabled.</noscript>


</body></html>